ASP-Completeness Proofs of Puzzles Using the T-Metacell Framework 
This paper utilizes the "T-metacell" framework to prove the ASP-completeness of **certain puzzles**.

The T-metacell framework uses grid graph Hamiltonicity to prove **a certain property** of puzzles.

Tang’s framework was recently used by **someone** to prove the NP-completeness of five puzzles. 
This paper utilizes the "T-metacell" framework to prove the ASP-completeness of four new pencil puzzles: Grand Tour, Entry Exit, Yagit, and Zahlenschlange.

The T-metacell framework uses grid graph Hamiltonicity to prove NP-hardness of puzzles.

Tang’s framework was recently used by Deurloo et al. to prove the NP-completeness of five puzzles.

