**********Source Check**********

The claim 'Something is a multi-agent-based interactive framework for mental health assessment.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The title of the paper is "AgentMental: An Interactive Multi-Agent Framework for Explainable and Adaptive Mental Health Assessment." The abstract and introduction also state: "in this paper, we propose a multi-agent framework for mental health evaluation" and "we propose a multi-agent-based interactive framework to simulate clinical interview scenarios for mental health assessment (AgentMental)". </accept>

**********Source Check**********

The claim 'The adaptive questioning mechanism in AgentMental aims to alleviate something.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The "Abstract" section states: "We introduce an adaptive questioning mechanism in which an evaluation agent assesses the adequacy of user responses to determine the necessity of generating targeted follow-up queries to address ambiguity and missing information." The "Introduction" section further elaborates: "Prior to score assignment, we use an adaptive questioning mechanism to alleviate the issue of insufficient information in user responses". The "Adaptive Question Generation" section also notes it "can detect vague, ambiguous, or incomplete responses and generate appropriate clarification questions to guide the conversation." This directly answers that it aims to alleviate ambiguity, missing information, and insufficient/vague/incomplete responses. </accept>

**********Source Check**********

The claim 'Comprehensive evaluations of AgentMental were conducted on something.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The text explicitly states in both the Abstract and Introduction sections that "In addition, we conduct comprehensive evaluations on the DAIC-WOZ dataset, and the results demonstrate that AgentMental consistently outperforms existing studies." The "Experimental Setting" section under "Experiments" further details the "Dataset" used, confirming it is the DAIC-WOZ dataset. </accept>

